# rite-server production image — the team-deployment shell (ADR 0004/0005).
#
# IT COMPILES NOTHING. The binary is built before this file is read, by a job per
# architecture on a runner of that architecture, and handed here as an artifact. This
# recipe is a base, a COPY and six lines of metadata.
#
# WHY THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. It used to carry three stages: bundle the frontend,
# compile the workspace, ship the result. Compiling inside the image meant compiling once
# per architecture, and the release builds both from one amd64 runner — so the arm64 half
# ran under QEMU. Measured on the 0.2.10 rehearsal: 49m52 for the dependency layer and
# 17m03 for the final build, against 7m00 and 3m21 for the same work native. Sixty-seven
# of the job's seventy-three minutes were emulation.
#
# Nothing here executes, so there is nothing to emulate: `COPY` is performed by the
# builder, not inside the target rootfs, and one amd64 runner assembles both architectures
# without QEMU at all.
#
# --chmod=0755 AND NOT A chmod LATER. Artifact upload does not keep the executable bit —
# "File permissions are not maintained during zipped artifact upload", files arrive 644 —
# so the binary would land here unrunnable and the image would fail at start with a
# permission error that says nothing about where it came from. The mode is set by the COPY
# itself, which also means no `RUN chmod` and therefore no emulation sneaking back in.
#
# THE GLIBC COUPLING MOVED, IT DID NOT GO AWAY. The binary used to be compiled on the same
# Debian it runs on, so the question answered itself. It is now compiled on a GitHub runner
# and run on the Debian below, and a binary cannot find a glibc older than the one it was
# linked against. The floor of the build runner must therefore be at or below the runtime
# base's. That is not visible in any single file, so `e2e/ci-image-check.mjs` holds the two
# ends together and fails when they drift.
#
# Build:  podman build -f Containerfile.server -t rite-server:local .
#         (after `cargo build --release -p rite-server`, with the binary placed at
#          dist/<amd64|arm64>/rite-server — the workflows do exactly this.)
# Run:    podman run --rm -p 1421:1421 rite-server:local

# WHAT THE SHIPPED SERVER RUNS ON. The tag is the hash of `Containerfile.runtime`, so the
# base and its recipe cannot drift apart unnoticed; the digest is what is actually pulled.
#
# THIS LINE IS THE PIN AND THERE IS NO SECOND COPY OF IT. A digest written in two places
# is a digest that will disagree with itself.
#
# What this base carries, so that nothing here has to: `ca-certificates` and the `rite`
# user with its home. Both used to run in this file — twice per release under emulation,
# and once per pull request, since CI builds this image too. They happen weekly now, when
# nobody is waiting.
FROM ghcr.io/altagen/rite-runtime:df96a51a6275-20261119@sha256:dfd3da4e5ea779b3b71c68fdd2b849e79418c71dec4088c0eaabc2810bcdcd2c AS runtime

# BuildKit sets TARGETARCH per platform: `amd64` or `arm64`, the same spelling the build
# jobs use for their artifact names. One COPY therefore serves both architectures, and a
# missing binary fails the build here rather than producing an image that cannot start.
ARG TARGETARCH
COPY --chmod=0755 dist/${TARGETARCH}/rite-server /usr/local/bin/rite-server

USER rite
# The home, and not the default `/`. A local terminal opened from the web UI inherits this
# process's working directory — nothing makes a shell go to $HOME on its own — so without
# this line a member landed in `/`, which they cannot write to and which holds nothing of
# theirs. The data volume mounts under here too, so the one directory a session can use is
# the one it starts in. `e2e/server-image-check.mjs` holds it, and the same line is in the
# acceptance fixture: the test image has to start a shell where the real one does.
WORKDIR /home/rite
# Bind all interfaces so the container is reachable; the vault lives under the
# rite user's data dir (mount a volume at /home/rite/.local/share/rite to persist).
ENV RITE_ADDR=0.0.0.0:1421
EXPOSE 1421
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/rite-server"]
